DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260926
SUMMARY:Deadline: University of Oxford: Postdoctoral Research Fellow in Com
 putational Social Science and Text Analysis (CeDR)
DESCRIPTION:The Centre for Democratic Resilience (CeDR) at the University o
 f Oxford is hiring a Postdoctoral Research Fellow in Computational Social 
 Science and Text Analysis to join an interdisciplinary team building a new
  computational research agenda on risks to academic freedom\, institutiona
 l autonomy\, and higher education governance. The fellow leads computation
 al analysis of large collections of legal\, regulatory\, and political tex
 ts\, developing innovative NLP methods to analyse legislation\, policy doc
 uments\, and political discourse\, with particular attention to Germany. R
 EQUIREMENTS: a doctorate (held or near completion) in political science or
  a related field\, with expertise in computational social science and natu
 ral language processing. TERMS: full-time\, fixed-term for three years\, b
 ased in Oxford\, salary GBP 39\,424 to 51\,983. APPLICATION: online via th
 e University of Oxford job pages with CV and supporting statement (job ref
 erence 188420)\; online interviews the week of 5 October 2026. Start 1 Nov
 ember 2026 or soon after. NOTE: this is a salaried research job\, not a gr
 ant. DEADLINE: 25 September 2026\, 12 noon UK time.\n\nOrganisation: Centr
 e for Democratic Resilience\, Department of Politics and International Rel
 ations\, University of Oxford\nLocation: Oxford\, UK (full-time\, on site)
 . Must hold or be close to completing a doctorate in political science or 
 a related field.\nAward: Salary GBP 39\,424 to 51\,983 per annum. Full-tim
 e\, fixed-term for three years. No application fee.\nDuration: 3 years\, s
 tarting 1 November 2026 or as soon as possible thereafter.\n\nMore: https:
 //www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DST162/postdoctoral-research-fellow-in-computational-
 social-science-and-text-analysis?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
URL:https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DST162/postdoctoral-research-fellow-in-compu
 tational-social-science-and-text-analysis?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Oxford\, UK (full-time\, on site). Must hold or be close to comple
 ting a doctorate in political science or a related field.
