DTSTAMP:20261008T193437Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261127
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261128
SUMMARY:Deadline: Open City Documentary Festival 2027 (Call for Entries)
DESCRIPTION:The 17th Open City Documentary Festival takes place at venues a
 cross London in April 2027\, presenting international contemporary and ret
 rospective non-fiction film\, audio and cross-media work alongside filmmak
 er Q&As\, panels\, talks and workshops. The festival nurtures experimentat
 ion within the expanded field of non-fiction cinema\, from artists' moving
  image to documentary\, the essay film\, audio and cross-media works\; rec
 ent artists screened include Sky Hopinka\, Onyeka Igwe\, Luke Fowler\, Ana
  Vaz\, Jessica Sarah Rinland and Morgan Quaintance. ELIGIBILITY: non-ficti
 on film and video\, cross-platform projects and audio works completed afte
 r 1 January 2026\; no strict premiere requirement\, but works not yet publ
 icly screened in London are prioritized. All selected filmmakers receive s
 creening fees: GBP 275 for works over 60 minutes\, GBP 140 for works over 
 40 minutes\, GBP 70 for works under 40 minutes\, GBP 100 for cross-platfor
 m projects (all incl. VAT). Submissions via FilmFreeway with tiered entry 
 fees (lower before the early deadline). EARLY DEADLINE: 25 September 2026.
  FINAL DEADLINE: 27 November 2026\; all entrants notified by 22 February 2
 027.\n\nOrganisation: Open City Documentary Festival / UCL\nLocation: Lond
 on\, UK\nAward: Screening fees for all selected works: GBP 275 for works o
 ver 60 min\, GBP 140 for works over 40 min\, GBP 70 for works under 40 min
 \, GBP 100 for cross-platform projects (all incl. VAT)\nDuration: Festival
  runs 9-18 April 2027 at venues across London\n\nMore: https://opencitylon
 don.com/entries/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://opencitylondon.com/entries/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:London\, UK
END:VEVENT
