SUMMARY:Deadline: rb&hArts: Organ Donation Artworks Commission 2026 (Royal 
 Brompton and Harefield Hospitals\, London)
DESCRIPTION:rb&hArts\, the arts programme of the Royal Brompton and Harefie
 ld hospitals (part of Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust)\, commiss
 ions one artist to create two permanent artworks\, one for each hospital\,
  exploring organ donation and transplantation through themes of hope\, gen
 erosity\, connection\, renewal and the gift of life. WHAT YOU GET: a GBP 9
 \,000 budget for the entire commission\, covering design\, production and 
 stakeholder engagement across both artworks. PROCESS: strong emphasis on c
 o-creation\; the artist works directly with patients\, transplant recipien
 ts\, donor families and clinical staff\, with rb&hArts organising stakehol
 der meetings\, workshops and interviews. ELIGIBILITY: the call states no r
 estrictions on who can apply\, though the participatory process happens on
  site in London. APPLICATION: by proposal via an online form linked from t
 he call listing. DEADLINE: 27 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: rb&hArts (R
 oyal Brompton and Harefield hospitals\, Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundatio
 n Trust)\nLocation: Royal Brompton Hospital (Chelsea\, London) and Harefie
 ld Hospital\, UK. No stated restrictions on who can apply\, but on-site co
 -creation implies UK-feasible artists.\nAward: GBP 9\,000 total budget for
  the two-artwork commission\, covering design\, production and stakeholder
  engagement. No application fee.\nDuration: Commission period not specifie
 d\; permanent artworks for both hospital sites.\n\nMore: https://www.artra
 bbit.com/artist-opportunities/2026/september/rbharts-artist-open-call-orga
 n-donation-artworks?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
URL:https://www.artrabbit.com/artist-opportunities/2026/september/rbharts-a
 rtist-open-call-organ-donation-artworks?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Royal Brompton Hospital (Chelsea\, London) and Harefield Hospital\
 , UK. No stated restrictions on who can apply\, but on-site co-creation im
 plies UK-feasible artists.
END:VEVENT
