UID:odi-researcher-ai-quantitative-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261008T193437Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261009
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261010
SUMMARY:Deadline: ODI Researcher (AI and Quantitative)\, London
DESCRIPTION:The Open Data Institute\, the London non-profit founded by Tim 
 Berners-Lee and Nigel Shadbolt\, is hiring a Researcher (AI and quantitati
 ve) in its Research and Development team. The role focuses on data-centric
  AI: benchmark creation and model evaluation\, and improving the AI readin
 ess of existing and emerging data infrastructures. DAY TO DAY: running rig
 orous experiments to evaluate model performance across technical metrics\;
  leading work packages covering corpus construction\, ground-truth curatio
 n\, task design\, evaluation harnesses\, statistical analysis and benchmar
 king reproducibility\; assessing public sector and government datasets for
  AI-readiness using ODI frameworks\; authoring peer-reviewed papers\, tech
 nical annexes\, reproducible code repositories\, blog posts and policy bri
 efings\; plus desk reviews\, literature reviews\, stakeholder mapping\, su
 rveys and interviews on data\, AI and technology topics. WHO THEY WANT: pr
 actical experience in data-centric AI methodologies including benchmark bu
 ilding and dataset quality assurance\; deep applied knowledge of LLMs\, RA
 G and agentic frameworks\; experience with evaluation protocols\, harness 
 design and comparative benchmarking across major open and closed-source mo
 del families\; proficiency in statistical modelling and ML workflows\; mix
 ed qualitative and quantitative research skills\; understanding of open sc
 ience and FAIR principles and of GDPR implications for research. Desirable
 : a track record of commissioned research or policy briefings for tech org
 anisations\, government bodies or foundations\, and knowledge of current d
 ebates in the data and open culture movements\, including the collection a
 nd use of data by AI systems. TO APPLY: upload a CV\, a cover letter\, and
  work samples including links (GitHub\, Hugging Face) to previous AI proje
 cts relevant to the position. Closing date Friday 9 October 2026. Question
 s to jobs@theodi.org.\n\nOrganisation: Open Data Institute (ODI)\nLocation
 : Kings Cross\, London\, UK (hybrid). 35 hours/week.\nAward: SALARIED JOB\
 , listed as a deliberate exception to the desk's no-jobs rule: GBP 39\,071
  per annum depending on experience\, plus benefits (5% contributory pensio
 n\, 30 days holiday plus bank holidays\, life assurance\, GBP 1\,250 annua
 l professional development budget after probation\, flexible working). Gra
 de 6\; a senior Grade 5 role may be offered depending on experience. No ap
 plication fee.\nDuration: 12-month fixed-term contract with possibility of
  extension\, renewal or switch to permanent.\n\nMore: https://theodi.livev
 acancies.co.uk/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral#
 /job/details/84
URL:https://theodi.livevacancies.co.uk/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral#/job/details/84
LOCATION:Kings Cross\, London\, UK (hybrid). 35 hours/week.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
